hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"131","Abdul Rahman bin Bishr bin Al-Hakam told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ata’ told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Close your door and mention the name of God, for Satan does not open closed, and turn off Your lamp, and mention the name of God, and your watering can, and mention the name of God, and the cover of your vessel, and mention the name of God, even if it is with a stick that you present to Him.”"
"132","Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr bin Khalifa, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us May God bless him and grant him peace: “Close your doors, cover your watering cans, cover your utensils, and put out your lamps, for Satan does not open anything, nor He loosens his cover and does not reveal his cover, and the worm may have set fire to the people of the household, so restrain your shepherds and your families when... “The sunset until the evening break.” Yusuf told us: The time for dinner, and this is a misrepresentation. Rather, it is the time for dinner, which is the deepening of the darkness. Abu Bakr said: In the report there is evidence that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, only ordered covering the utensils and placing the watering cans, as Satan does not loosen the waterskin, nor remove the cover of the vessel, because not covering the vessel is a disobedience to God Almighty, nor does the water become impure. By not covering the vessel, since the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, knew that if Satan found a water-skin not brought to him, he would drink from it. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the waterskin to be tied and the vessel to be covered, he knew that if Satan found the waterskin other than a waterskin, he would drink from it. This was evidence that if he found the vessel not covered, he drank from it. Tell us the news that you mentioned about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, informing him if he found a waterskin other than a water bottle, he drank from it."
"133","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Karim al-San’ani Abu Hisham, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Aqeel bin Maqil bin Munabbih, on the authority of His father, Uqail, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, said: This is what I asked Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari about, and he told me: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say: “Tighten the watering holes, and close the doors when you lie down at night, and leave your food and drink, for Satan will come.” If he did not find the door closed, he entered it, and if he did not find a water-skin, he drank from it, and if he found the door closed, and the water-skin was a water-taker, he did not allow him to drink from it. And it has not been opened and closed, and if any of you cannot find a vessel with which to brew, let him offer him a stick.” We only began by mentioning the siwak before performing ablution, because the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, began with it before performing ablution when entering his house."
